1
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:40,248
They're trying to kill me! They're crazy!

2
00:00:41,917 --> 00:00:43,960
Calm down, Sally. You're safe now.

3
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:45,753
Can you tell me what happened?

4
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:47,839
We ran out of gas.

5
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:49,590
Kirk went to get help.

6
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:54,971
Hello?

7
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:58,099
Is anybody there?

8
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:12,613
Kirk!

9
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:35,636
Kirk?

10
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:56,657
Jerry!

11
00:01:57,493 --> 00:01:59,827
Sally, I hear something. Stop!

12
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:19,347
No! Please!

13
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:21,849
Please! Please stop!

14
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:27,688
Give me that hammer!

15
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:06,102
<i>Sheriff, we've got the victim's statement.
She's on her way to the hospital.</i>

16
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,520
<i>What's your location?</i>

17
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:09,814
Quick Hill Road. I'm headed there.

18
00:03:10,065 --> 00:03:12,900
Send an ambulance in case
there are any other survivors.

19
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,777
<i>Hello, Sheriff. It's Marvin.</i>

20
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:17,113
<i>I'm two minutes away and closing in.</i>

21
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:18,781
<i>All right, step on it, Marvin.</i>

22
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:23,828
Sheriff, that family is probably armed.
Are you going to wait for backup?

23
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:26,455
<i>I can't wait. I'm going in.</i>

24
00:03:33,839 --> 00:03:35,423
-Oh, God.
-Come on, let's go.

25
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:36,674
Shit.

26
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:48,519
<i>The sheriff wants an ambulance
at 647 Quick Hill Road.</i>

27
00:03:48,604 --> 00:03:49,645
<i>Do you copy?</i>

28
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:57,111
Drayton?

29
00:03:58,196 --> 00:04:01,949
You know why I'm here! Come
out and bring your boy, Jed.

30
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:03,618
Hands on your head.

31
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:08,164
I'm not leaving, Drayton.

32
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:12,001
There's a young woman who
says they killed her friends.

33
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:14,795
Nobody's going to turn a blind eye to this.

34
00:04:20,344 --> 00:04:22,637
He protects the house and the family.

35
00:04:23,055 --> 00:04:24,639
That's not what I heard.

36
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:40,321
Goddamn it. Come on out!

37
00:04:40,739 --> 00:04:42,698
I'm not waiting here all day.

38
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,992
I'll call the state police
if that's what you want.

39
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:47,995
Turn the boy over, Drayton!

40
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:51,457
This doesn't have to get any
harder than it already is.

41
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:53,584
-You're not taking anyone from this family.
-Don't make it worse.

42
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:56,545
I'm not leaving without the boy, Drayton.

43
00:04:56,672 --> 00:04:57,755
-We're Sawyers!
-Sure you are!

44
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,173
What are you going to do?

45
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:01,133
Do what you have to, Sheriff!

46
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:02,259
Turn over the boy!

47
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:08,933
Give him the boy. He's an idiot anyway.

48
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:10,851
He's family.

49
00:05:32,207 --> 00:05:33,874
We're going to hand Jed over.

50
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:37,044
All right. Bring him out.

51
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,046
Hold on, Marvin.

52
00:05:40,215 --> 00:05:41,716
Make sure he gets a good lawyer!

53
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:43,634
Done.

54
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:46,387
This is your fault, boy!

55
00:05:47,431 --> 00:05:48,889
You let that bitch get away.

56
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,604
Shit.

57
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,319
Come here, Sawyer!

58
00:06:02,404 --> 00:06:03,654
Give us the retard!

59
00:06:06,742 --> 00:06:08,659
More of them are here! Those aren't cops.

60
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,580
Get back, Drayton!

61
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:13,664
We've got trouble!

62
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:21,005
-Stay out of this, Burt. I've got it under control.
-We came to help.

63
00:06:21,256 --> 00:06:23,257
Then start by making everybody
get back in their cars

64
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,467
and get the hell out of here.

65
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:25,593
That's not going to happen.

66
00:06:25,761 --> 00:06:28,429
Come on, boys! Let's lynch
these sons of bitches.

67
00:06:28,597 --> 00:06:30,765
I've got this under control.
He's turning over the boy.

68
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:33,100
What's going on in there, Sheriff?

69
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:35,853
-Kick him out!
-He's handing over his son.

70
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,480
Bring him out!

71
00:06:37,606 --> 00:06:39,857
-Burn them, Ollie!
-Special delivery!

72
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:41,650
No!

73
00:06:41,777 --> 00:06:42,777
You bastards!

74
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:36,497
That's it. A Sawyer bonfire.

75
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:39,166
You're responsible for this, Burt.

76
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,921
An eye for an eye, Sheriff.
Nobody escapes biblical justice.

77
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:49,552
That's right, boys!

78
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:07,736
Keep looking. It's hard to find
them when they're burned to a crisp.

79
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,532
Hell. Burt!

80
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,369
-Yeah?
-Look at this.

81
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,706
I'm going to hang this thing up in the bar.

82
00:08:20,542 --> 00:08:22,293
-This beauty's coming with me.
-We'll be heroes.

83
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,978
Son of a bitch.

84
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:42,938
Help us.

85
00:08:44,608 --> 00:08:47,067
Yeah. Come here.

86
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:49,653
Come on. Come here.

87
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,572
Come on. Let her go.

88
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,575
Come on. Yeah.

89
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,162
I've got her. Easy now.

90
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:05,085
Easy.

91
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:17,264
Gavin, where have you been? What is...?

92
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:19,266
Oh, my God. It's a baby.

93
00:09:19,351 --> 00:09:21,268
I found her. I got her out of the woods.

94
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,020
Gavin!

95
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:26,148
-Come on, we're going to be in the paper.
-Yeah, I'll be right there.

96
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,150
Yeah.

97
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:30,569
Come on, you're going to miss it!

98
00:09:30,654 --> 00:09:32,488
She got burned.

99
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:34,490
All right. Yeah, brother!

100
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:36,200
I'm coming, buddy!

101
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:38,702
-We're keeping her, right?
-I brought her for you, Arlene.

102
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:41,330
You never know what you look
like until you see the picture.

103
00:10:18,994 --> 00:10:19,994
I'll be right back.

104
00:10:24,708 --> 00:10:26,583
What were you thinking?

105
00:10:26,668 --> 00:10:29,378
It was Ryan's idea. I warned you.

106
00:10:29,504 --> 00:10:32,089
Next time your sleazy
boyfriend tries to set me up

107
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:33,841
with one of his high-school buddies,

108
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:37,720
-give him a kiss for me.
-What?

109
00:10:37,846 --> 00:10:40,180
I like him. We got along.

110
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:43,892
We started talking, and he made
me some delicious pancakes.

111
00:10:44,019 --> 00:10:45,311
Excellent.

112
00:10:45,395 --> 00:10:47,271
He wants to be a chef.

113
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:50,607
And he's much more interesting than he looks.

114
00:10:50,692 --> 00:10:53,569
Can you handle the four-day
trip to New Orleans with him?

115
00:10:53,737 --> 00:10:56,530
I got you beat, girl. He
even offered to drive.

116
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:58,949
-Really? Wow.
-You bet!

117
00:10:59,034 --> 00:11:00,534
-I was talking to...
-Nikki!

118
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:02,536
Bobby wants you back at the register.

119
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:06,415
Fine. I'm going to get my
Halloween costume ready.

120
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,208
And it won't be scary at all.

121
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,611
Nikki likes your friend from high school.

122
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,613
Something about pancakes?

123
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:38,822
That's Kenny's famous trick.

124
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:41,408
Nikki never stood a chance.

125
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,081
I thought we weren't bringing work home.

126
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:49,333
Do you think I'm crazy?

127
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:53,754
No, but you should broaden your interests.

128
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,508
Come work up a sweat.

129
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,593
I don't want any bruises.

130
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:01,595
I wasn't talking about the punching bag.

131
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:03,931
Neither was I.

132
00:12:18,113 --> 00:12:19,780
I love your strange birthmark.

133
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:27,621
-Damn it.
-Who is it?

134
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:31,291
Shit. It could be my contract.

135
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:37,631
Coming!

136
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:56,024
-It's for you.
-For me?

137
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,485
From a law firm in Dallas.

138
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:05,909
My grandmother died three weeks ago.

139
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:08,078
I thought you didn't have
any living grandparents.

140
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:09,538
So did I.

141
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,125
I just wanted to have a baby.

142
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:14,918
-Enough.
-I wanted children so badly,

143
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:17,337
-but I couldn't have them!
-Enough, Arlene.

144
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,175
Why didn't you tell me?

145
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:24,178
Tell you what? That your
mother has a defective uterus?

146
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,514
I wanted a child. Period.

147
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,934
So what? Aren't we good enough for you?

148
00:13:31,019 --> 00:13:32,019
I didn't say that.

149
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:36,356
I just want to know where I
come from, and who my family is.

150
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:40,694
Well, we raised you. And I'd
say you were pretty lucky.

151
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:42,529
Those people were...

152
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,740
I can't even describe them.

153
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:46,575
-Shut up, Arlene.
-There are no words, Heather.

154
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:47,701
Shut up!

155
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:53,290
You come from a pile of shit.

156
00:13:55,627 --> 00:13:57,419
There. Now you know.

157
00:13:58,213 --> 00:14:00,214
If I'd been smart, I'd have left you there.

158
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:06,720
I'm leaving! I've had enough.

159
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:08,055
Don't you dare go there!

160
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:09,139
Heather!

161
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:12,684
Heather.

162
00:14:14,062 --> 00:14:17,314
Heather, if you go there,
you'll bring trouble on us.

163
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:18,774
What are you talking about?

164
00:14:20,235 --> 00:14:21,235
Trust me.

165
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:25,030
Newt, Texas, is the last
place you want to be.

166
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,594
-How'd it go?
-Awful.

167
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:51,557
It sucks finding out your parents
lied to you your whole life.

168
00:14:52,058 --> 00:14:53,141
I'm sorry, honey.

169
00:14:53,268 --> 00:14:54,476
I'm adopted.

170
00:14:58,106 --> 00:14:59,982
I've never felt comfortable around them.

171
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,944
I'm going to pack

172
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,946
-for Texas, not New Orleans.
-Wait.

173
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,948
-Wait.
-No, Ryan. I have to go.

174
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:10,033
-Forget Halloween.
-Please listen to me.

175
00:15:10,118 --> 00:15:11,118
Hey.

176
00:15:14,956 --> 00:15:16,873
Ryan called us.

177
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:19,585
-Kenny!
-I love your artwork.

178
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:23,922
I figured you'd want to sort out
your grandmother's affairs, so...

179
00:15:24,007 --> 00:15:25,882
Knowing how stubborn you are,

180
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:27,843
we decided to go with you.

181
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:30,095
Really? You'd do that?

182
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,346
Are you kidding?

183
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:35,976
Come here. Of course! You're our friend.

184
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:40,272
I wasn't going to let you
go alone to some hick town.

185
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:44,568
I don't mind driving to Texas.
I hear the barbecue's amazing.

186
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:47,404
What do you think?

187
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:49,781
Okay. Sounds like a good plan.

188
00:15:50,158 --> 00:15:51,742
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

189
00:16:12,055 --> 00:16:13,055
Texas, here we come!

190
00:16:18,144 --> 00:16:22,022
Oh, my God. Can you believe this? Oh, my God.

191
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,315
Go!

192
00:16:31,908 --> 00:16:33,408
-What did you get?
-All this.

193
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:36,953
You like it? Because it cost me 25 dollars.

194
00:16:37,038 --> 00:16:38,830
No way. That's a rip-off.

195
00:16:39,082 --> 00:16:41,792
Don't worry, honey. I used your credit card.

196
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:44,836
Yeah? That's fine. Know why?

197
00:16:45,338 --> 00:16:46,338
Because

198
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,050
-Kenny paid for the gas.
-What?

199
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:51,677
What...? Give me that.

200
00:16:51,761 --> 00:16:53,637
-How'd you get that out of my pocket?
-Kenny.

201
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:55,555
-Don't cry.
-It's okay. Let's go, babe.

202
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,517
-Ready?
-Let's go, babe.

203
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:04,189
What was that?

204
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:09,361
Jeez, are you okay?

205
00:17:10,113 --> 00:17:11,113
Oh, God.

206
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:12,614
-Yeah, I'm fine.
-You hit him, Kenny.

207
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:16,243
Sorry, I didn't see you.

208
00:17:16,327 --> 00:17:17,327
I'm fine.

209
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:21,206
I ought to sue you.

210
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,543
I'll settle for a beef jerky stick.

211
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:29,047
Where are you headed?

212
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:30,632
New Orleans.

213
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:32,843
You're kidding! Awesome!

214
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:34,803
-You headed there too?
-Nah.

215
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,222
Shreveport? It's on the way.

216
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,266
What about your car? Did it break down?

217
00:17:39,726 --> 00:17:42,185
It's a long story.

218
00:17:42,687 --> 00:17:43,812
Long story short,

219
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:46,982
my girlfriend kicked me out, and
I've been hitchhiking since Tulsa.

220
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:49,776
I'd really appreciate a ride.

221
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:53,155
I don't mind paying you.

222
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:54,614
Sixty bucks.

223
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,451
You'd be doing me a big favor.
It'd really help me out.

224
00:17:58,453 --> 00:17:59,453
In this rain?

225
00:18:00,163 --> 00:18:01,830
-All right. Let's go.
-Really?

226
00:18:02,999 --> 00:18:04,875
We have to make a stop in Texas on the way.

227
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:07,085
Beats walking.

228
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:08,920
Okay.

229
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,894
WELCOME TO TEXAS
DRIVE FRIENDLY — THE TEXAS WAY

230
00:18:42,705 --> 00:18:43,705
Are you okay?

231
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:46,666
Yeah. I'm fine.

232
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:51,296
-Are you scared?
-No.

233
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:56,843
-I just want to know where I belong.
-Yeah.

234
00:18:59,514 --> 00:19:00,514
What's in Newt?

235
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,226
A one-sided family reunion.

236
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:08,188
My grandmother died. I
have to sign some papers.

237
00:19:08,523 --> 00:19:11,983
I'm sorry for your loss. Were you close?

238
00:19:12,193 --> 00:19:16,154
I only found out she existed
yesterday. But family is family.

239
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:17,572
Amen, sister.

240
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:25,413
Family is complicated. Blood
ties are the strongest.

241
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:38,510
WELCOME TO NEWT
Population: 2,306

242
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,612
Do you know anything about this place?

243
00:19:58,906 --> 00:19:59,906
I've only got the address.

244
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:01,867
We get in and get out, right?

245
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,535
That's the plan.

246
00:20:05,121 --> 00:20:06,454
We'd have been lost if it was dark.

247
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:08,707
What the hell? We wouldn't have seen a thing.

248
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:12,377
This is it. Homestead Road. Turn left.

249
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:13,753
HOMESTEAD ROAD
CALDWELL ROAD

250
00:20:25,141 --> 00:20:26,141
This can't be it, can it?

251
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,268
He said there'd be a big gate.

252
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:38,403
Wow.

253
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,365
There must be something back there.

254
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:43,783
Like a castle.

255
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:45,827
Okay.

256
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:15,815
Mr. Farnsworth? I'm Heather.

257
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:19,194
I recognized the car. It's identical.

258
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:20,654
Thanks for coming all the way from Dallas.

259
00:21:21,197 --> 00:21:25,158
Anything for Verna. She was
a good woman. A great person.

260
00:21:26,369 --> 00:21:28,328
Though she wasn't very popular in this town.

261
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:29,454
BITCH

262
00:21:30,581 --> 00:21:32,874
I didn't realize you were bringing friends.

263
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:34,292
Is that a problem?

264
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:38,463
The house is yours, if you want it.

265
00:21:39,674 --> 00:21:40,966
You should know

266
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:43,677
Verna's trust prohibits you from selling it.

267
00:21:44,095 --> 00:21:45,512
These documents explain everything.

268
00:21:45,596 --> 00:21:47,180
Okay. Thank you.

269
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:50,684
You can't see the house from here.

270
00:21:51,352 --> 00:21:54,187
But it's behind that grove of trees.

271
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:01,778
These keys open everything inside and out.

272
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,406
Verna took security seriously.

273
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:09,953
Zero-eight-one-nine.

274
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,747
It's easier to remember as a date.

275
00:22:12,999 --> 00:22:13,999
August nineteenth.

276
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:17,002
Right. The gate opens
automatically from the other side.

277
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:20,880
-I have a house.
-And a whole list of assets

278
00:22:20,965 --> 00:22:24,342
which I'll send as soon as
the accountants sign off.

279
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:27,846
I almost forgot.

280
00:22:29,223 --> 00:22:30,515
The most important thing.

281
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:35,311
-It's from Verna. Make sure you read it.
-Okay. I will.

282
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:39,149
And call me if you have any questions.

283
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:42,902
Aren't you coming in?

284
00:22:46,073 --> 00:22:48,783
No. I have other people waiting for me.

285
00:22:48,868 --> 00:22:50,368
Don't forget to read Verna's letter.

286
00:22:51,829 --> 00:22:52,829
Sir?

287
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:54,706
How did you find me?

288
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:58,293
Find you? Honey, you were never lost.

289
00:23:44,006 --> 00:23:45,632
It's a mansion! Oh, my God!

290
00:23:52,515 --> 00:23:55,266
-Wow.
-Amazing.

291
00:23:55,726 --> 00:23:59,646
-Unbelievable. Oh, my God! Are you serious?
-Wow.

292
00:24:00,523 --> 00:24:01,856
It's even prettier on the inside.

293
00:24:03,192 --> 00:24:05,276
-I don't know where to start.
-How about here?

294
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:13,952
-What are you doing?
-Wow.

295
00:24:14,537 --> 00:24:15,703
Look at that fancy china.

296
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:20,375
-Heather, can I open this door?
-Yeah.

297
00:24:22,837 --> 00:24:24,629
-Wow.
-Wow.

298
00:24:26,674 --> 00:24:28,591
Makes you want to come home again.

299
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:29,717
Anybody want some tea?

300
00:24:30,469 --> 00:24:31,553
It's all set up.

301
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:35,849
Heather, what did Grandma do for a living?

302
00:24:36,559 --> 00:24:37,976
I have no idea.

303
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:39,936
Look at this!

304
00:24:43,315 --> 00:24:44,983
Looks like Grandma liked pool.

305
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:47,819
<i>-Who wants to play?
-Me.</i>

306
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:50,864
-You got any money, bitch?
-I'm a bitch now?

307
00:24:50,948 --> 00:24:52,157
Yeah, my bitch.

308
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:53,616
Rack 'em up.

309
00:24:53,701 --> 00:24:55,368
-Rack up what?
-The balls.

310
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:02,292
-All right.
-Nice shot.

311
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:04,794
Too bad.

312
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:07,172
Ow!

313
00:25:07,256 --> 00:25:09,841
All right. Want to see me play? I'm
going to own you. Where's the cue ball?

314
00:25:57,348 --> 00:25:59,182
ELI THEODORE SAWYER
AUGUST 19

315
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,120
Thank you.

316
00:26:32,925 --> 00:26:36,177
LORETTA SISSY SAWYER
Beloved Daughter — AUGUST 19

317
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:43,184
What's wrong?

318
00:26:43,269 --> 00:26:47,355
This house is amazing! God, let's
spend the night here. It's fantastic.

319
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:50,692
That kitchen is fabulous. You
have to let me cook dinner.

320
00:26:50,818 --> 00:26:52,193
Yeah. And thank Darryl.

321
00:26:52,695 --> 00:26:54,862
He's paying for the steaks, right?

322
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:57,907
Shreveport can wait. I've needed
something like this for a long time.

323
00:26:58,284 --> 00:26:59,284
Thanks, guys.

324
00:26:59,994 --> 00:27:01,619
God, isn't he a Boy Scout?

325
00:27:02,413 --> 00:27:03,413
Come on.

326
00:27:03,497 --> 00:27:05,290
No, I'm the odd man out on this mission.

327
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:08,084
I'll bring down the bags
and do some cleaning.

328
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,735
Yeah, I'm a regular Boy Scout.

329
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:15,234
All right. Let's split up to save time.

330
00:28:15,319 --> 00:28:16,736
Would you buy that for me?

331
00:28:23,744 --> 00:28:25,328
See you in a few weeks, Mayor.

332
00:28:27,623 --> 00:28:31,584
Burt. Wish I had a hammock
like that in my backyard.

333
00:28:31,794 --> 00:28:33,169
Yeah, she's a beauty.

334
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,505
Hello, gorgeous.

335
00:28:45,057 --> 00:28:46,057
Come on, sweetheart.

336
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:52,855
What door are you opening?

337
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:55,483
Just one more thing and I'm done.

338
00:28:56,402 --> 00:28:58,111
-All right. I'll wait outside.
-Great.

339
00:28:58,195 --> 00:29:00,613
Is there a fair in town?

340
00:29:06,245 --> 00:29:08,246
-I'll check the price.
-What the hell are you doing?

341
00:29:09,164 --> 00:29:10,164
Nobody can see us.

342
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:12,667
It happened once.

343
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:16,379
Once. And I was completely wasted. Come on.

344
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,090
Come on. You begged me.

345
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:23,553
And now I'm begging you
not to touch my shirt.

346
00:29:26,223 --> 00:29:27,765
-Fine.
-Okay.

347
00:30:23,489 --> 00:30:26,908
A nice big door for a nice big key.

348
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,541
Found your hiding place, old lady.

349
00:30:41,507 --> 00:30:43,007
What do I need bottles of wine for?

350
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:55,895
What the hell is this?

351
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:07,823
Here we go. Come on.

352
00:31:10,786 --> 00:31:12,036
Come on!

353
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:14,580
I know how to handle stubborn bitches.

354
00:31:15,666 --> 00:31:17,959
All it takes is a few kicks.

355
00:31:18,961 --> 00:31:20,002
Come on, baby.

356
00:31:30,889 --> 00:31:33,849
I'll be back. I don't give up that easily!

357
00:32:05,173 --> 00:32:06,591
You're making things hard on yourself.

358
00:32:08,802 --> 00:32:10,678
That stuff wouldn't burn
with a tanker full of gas.

359
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,765
This one will give you a nice flavor.

360
00:32:15,309 --> 00:32:19,604
But if you want a raging fire, take this one.

361
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,440
Good to know.

362
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,320
You here for the fair?

363
00:32:29,239 --> 00:32:30,531
To break in a new house.

364
00:32:32,868 --> 00:32:36,078
Don't make too much noise. I
wouldn't want to have to arrest you.

365
00:32:36,622 --> 00:32:37,788
I'll try to behave.

366
00:32:38,915 --> 00:32:40,541
-How much is it?
-Nine dollars.

367
00:32:40,626 --> 00:32:41,834
Where's the party?

368
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:45,212
On Homestead Road.

369
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:47,757
The only place there is the Carson house.

370
00:32:48,258 --> 00:32:49,258
That's the one.

371
00:32:49,926 --> 00:32:51,135
I thought it was vacant.

372
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:52,470
Not anymore.

373
00:32:52,638 --> 00:32:54,096
Is the officer bothering you?

374
00:32:55,474 --> 00:32:57,224
If he is, I'll shoot him.

375
00:32:57,309 --> 00:32:58,476
I'm sure you would.

376
00:32:59,144 --> 00:33:00,144
Go check some parking meters.

377
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:08,527
Burt Hartman, proud mayor of this
little paradise. How are you?

378
00:33:10,155 --> 00:33:11,155
Heather.

379
00:33:11,239 --> 00:33:12,239
Pleased to meet you, Heather.

380
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,992
My hearing isn't so good anymore,

381
00:33:15,077 --> 00:33:17,787
but I could've sworn I heard
you mention the Carson house.

382
00:33:18,664 --> 00:33:19,664
I inherited it.

383
00:33:20,666 --> 00:33:22,917
-You're a Carson?
-No.

384
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:26,379
-You're not a Sawyer.
-Yes, I am.

385
00:33:28,298 --> 00:33:29,507
Yes, you've got their eyes.

386
00:33:29,591 --> 00:33:30,591
Did you know her?

387
00:33:30,676 --> 00:33:32,885
Yeah. Your family and I go way back.

388
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:36,305
And I know they wouldn't want
you stuck with that rundown dump.

389
00:33:36,390 --> 00:33:39,642
I'll make you a deal. I'll buy the house.

390
00:33:39,893 --> 00:33:40,893
No, thank you.

391
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:43,813
Oh, you're going to play hard to
get. Hell, I like you already.

392
00:33:44,064 --> 00:33:45,064
Let's go.

393
00:33:45,357 --> 00:33:46,732
Come on. Name your price.

394
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,241
Hello!

395
00:33:57,119 --> 00:33:59,078
-Shit.
-What?

396
00:33:59,413 --> 00:34:00,413
That damn thief.

397
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:04,500
He took my keys.

398
00:34:06,086 --> 00:34:08,421
Wow, he really fooled us. Seriously.

399
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:09,714
We never should've picked him up.

400
00:34:09,923 --> 00:34:10,923
Hey!

401
00:34:12,843 --> 00:34:13,843
Let's do this right.

402
00:34:15,721 --> 00:34:17,638
-What's going on?
-Darryl robbed us.

403
00:34:18,765 --> 00:34:21,100
He took some ashtrays and candlesticks.

404
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:24,687
Don't let that ruin your night. Come on.

405
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:26,522
-Cheers, guys.
-Yeah.

406
00:34:26,982 --> 00:34:27,982
To happiness.

407
00:34:28,358 --> 00:34:31,485
-To the queen.
-Yeah.

408
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:33,946
-To the Sawyers.
-To the Sawyers.

409
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,448
Sawyer. All right.

410
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:06,872
There's a whole dining set in here!

411
00:36:57,132 --> 00:37:05,222
Darryl?

412
00:37:10,395 --> 00:37:28,495
Darryl!

413
00:38:14,626 --> 00:38:16,377
-Oh, my God! You have to see this!
-What?

414
00:38:16,962 --> 00:38:19,129
It's disgusting! Hurry up!

415
00:38:19,214 --> 00:38:20,214
Hurry!

416
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:27,554
-It's down here.
-Where?

417
00:38:27,639 --> 00:38:30,516
-In that shed, right there.
-In here?

418
00:38:30,767 --> 00:38:31,767
God!

419
00:38:33,979 --> 00:38:34,979
Nikki, I can't see anything.

420
00:38:35,063 --> 00:38:37,106
It's under that bucket over there.

421
00:38:38,525 --> 00:38:39,858
It's under that bucket.

422
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:42,319
All right.

423
00:38:50,996 --> 00:38:52,162
What the hell is wrong with you, Nikki?

424
00:38:54,082 --> 00:38:55,082
What are you doing?

425
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:03,173
I told you it was disgusting.

426
00:40:01,816 --> 00:40:06,278
Ryan!

427
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:09,948
Guys!

428
00:40:17,332 --> 00:40:18,332
Kenny?

429
00:44:42,805 --> 00:44:43,805
What...?

430
00:44:45,016 --> 00:44:47,684
What's that? What is he doing?

431
00:44:49,062 --> 00:44:50,062
Who is that?

432
00:44:51,522 --> 00:44:59,196
Hey!

433
00:45:01,866 --> 00:45:02,866
-Run.
-What?

434
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:04,034
-Oh, my God!
-Run!

435
00:45:10,041 --> 00:45:11,750
-Hurry!
-Close the door!

436
00:45:40,780 --> 00:45:42,531
Welcome to Texas, asshole!

437
00:45:49,705 --> 00:45:50,705
Did you hit him?

438
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:52,290
I don't know.

439
00:45:52,625 --> 00:45:53,959
-Did you hit him?
-I don't know!

440
00:45:57,964 --> 00:45:59,089
Something's coming. Back up.

441
00:45:59,465 --> 00:46:00,882
Back up, Nikki!

442
00:46:03,886 --> 00:46:05,303
-Get in the van!
-It's Heather!

443
00:46:06,139 --> 00:46:09,558
-Move over!
-Let me in! Hurry, get us out of here!

444
00:46:09,642 --> 00:46:25,157
Hurry!

445
00:46:26,576 --> 00:46:27,742
What the hell was that?

446
00:46:30,621 --> 00:46:31,955
Where's Kenny?

447
00:46:32,999 --> 00:46:34,499
He's dead. They're fucking dead!

448
00:46:40,673 --> 00:46:43,467
Ryan, slow down! The gate has to open!

449
00:46:43,676 --> 00:46:45,177
-Give it time!
-We have to get out.

450
00:46:45,261 --> 00:46:46,595
Screw the gate! Seat belts!

451
00:46:55,521 --> 00:46:57,272
-What happened?
-The car stalled.

452
00:46:57,356 --> 00:46:58,356
Why?

453
00:46:58,608 --> 00:47:00,317
Okay. Back up.

454
00:47:03,696 --> 00:47:05,489
-Ryan!
-Back up!

455
00:47:05,698 --> 00:47:07,324
-Put it in reverse!
-What's wrong with it?

456
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:09,201
-Ryan, hurry!
-I'm fucking trying!

457
00:47:10,328 --> 00:47:11,328
It won't start!

458
00:47:13,331 --> 00:47:14,873
Shit!

459
00:47:14,999 --> 00:47:17,125
-Back up!
-Here we go.

460
00:47:21,797 --> 00:47:23,798
Wait for the gate to open.

461
00:47:25,218 --> 00:47:26,968
-Shit!
-Ryan!

462
00:47:27,053 --> 00:47:28,053
Ryan! Start it!

463
00:47:29,555 --> 00:47:31,473
-Hurry, Ryan!
-It won't start!

464
00:47:32,808 --> 00:47:34,309
Now! Hurry!

465
00:47:34,727 --> 00:47:36,394
-Ryan, hurry!
-Ryan, hurry!

466
00:47:36,687 --> 00:47:38,230
-Ryan, hurry!
-Come on!

467
00:47:38,314 --> 00:47:39,856
-Hurry!
-Please, hurry!

468
00:47:40,983 --> 00:47:41,983
Come on!

469
00:47:50,743 --> 00:47:52,035
Here he comes!

470
00:48:15,226 --> 00:48:18,562
Ryan.

471
00:48:44,922 --> 00:48:46,923
Heather, what happened?

472
00:48:51,637 --> 00:48:56,308
-What?
-Quiet.

473
00:49:00,855 --> 00:49:04,316
We have to get out of here right now!

474
00:49:12,825 --> 00:49:15,827
Get back, he's coming this way!

475
00:49:20,207 --> 00:49:21,207
My leg.

476
00:49:23,544 --> 00:49:24,586
No, Nikki!

477
00:49:57,787 --> 00:50:00,372
Fucking redneck!

478
00:50:39,578 --> 00:50:40,578
Run!

479
00:50:47,670 --> 00:50:49,337
You want to play?

480
00:50:51,507 --> 00:50:52,674
Call the police!

481
00:50:57,972 --> 00:50:59,139
Get out of the way!

482
00:50:59,306 --> 00:51:00,306
Call the police!

483
00:51:03,102 --> 00:51:04,936
-Hurry! Get out of the way!
-What the hell?

484
00:51:48,981 --> 00:51:49,981
Drop the damn saw!

485
00:51:51,484 --> 00:51:52,525
I said drop it!

486
00:51:52,651 --> 00:51:53,651
Put it down!

487
00:52:15,591 --> 00:52:16,591
Where's the girl?

488
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:18,843
-Carl's taking care of her in the back.
-All right.

489
00:52:27,228 --> 00:52:29,979
<i>Sheriff? It's Marvin. I'm at the crash site.</i>

490
00:52:30,064 --> 00:52:32,190
<i>-Do you copy?
-Go ahead, Marvin.</i>

491
00:52:32,733 --> 00:52:33,775
I'm approaching the vehicle.

492
00:52:34,610 --> 00:52:37,028
An old VW van on its side.

493
00:52:39,198 --> 00:52:40,198
It's completely wrecked.

494
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:43,243
<i>-Do you need an ambulance?
-I'm checking.</i>

495
00:52:46,539 --> 00:52:47,539
Negative.

496
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:48,915
No victims at the scene.

497
00:52:50,292 --> 00:52:53,586
Sheriff? There's blood everywhere.

498
00:52:54,380 --> 00:52:58,132
The seat's been cut up with
a saw. Someone died here.

499
00:52:58,759 --> 00:53:01,177
All right, stay where you are,
Marvin. I'll call you right back.

500
00:53:01,470 --> 00:53:02,470
Copy that.

501
00:53:19,196 --> 00:53:21,781
-Hi.
-Did you find her?

502
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:24,242
We'll find her.

503
00:53:26,620 --> 00:53:29,330
-I brought you a shirt.
-Thanks.

504
00:53:29,498 --> 00:53:30,498
At least it's clean.

505
00:53:34,086 --> 00:53:35,461
I shouldn't have brought them here.

506
00:53:38,465 --> 00:53:40,592
This town isn't much,

507
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:42,260
but we take care of our own.

508
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:44,512
By sunrise, he'll be good and dead.

509
00:53:45,639 --> 00:53:46,973
You can count on that.

510
00:53:48,392 --> 00:53:49,392
Carl!

511
00:53:53,397 --> 00:53:55,940
-Take your time.
-Okay.

512
00:54:06,744 --> 00:54:09,621
-Sheriff Hooper? This is Heather.
-Hello.

513
00:54:09,705 --> 00:54:11,789
-You're the girl he was chasing?
-Yes.

514
00:54:11,957 --> 00:54:14,208
He killed my friends, but Nikki

515
00:54:15,002 --> 00:54:16,669
survived the crash.

516
00:54:16,754 --> 00:54:18,630
We're investigating, but
there was nobody there.

517
00:54:18,714 --> 00:54:20,882
No, I left her there. He must've taken them.

518
00:54:20,966 --> 00:54:22,091
Do you know who he is?

519
00:54:22,176 --> 00:54:25,303
No. He was in the house, he was...

520
00:54:25,387 --> 00:54:27,639
-What house?
-The Carson estate.

521
00:54:29,558 --> 00:54:31,684
My grandmother left it to me. Verna Carson.

522
00:54:32,436 --> 00:54:33,937
We only got here a few hours ago.

523
00:54:35,439 --> 00:54:37,357
My last name is Sawyer, in
case you were going to ask.

524
00:54:37,524 --> 00:54:39,776
Sheriff, I dug around in the evidence room.

525
00:54:40,194 --> 00:54:41,694
I brought everything we have on Verna Carson.

526
00:54:42,738 --> 00:54:44,280
And a thick file on the Sawyers.

527
00:54:44,365 --> 00:54:45,823
Did you get a good look at him?

528
00:54:46,158 --> 00:54:47,367
He was wearing a face.

529
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:49,160
A mask?

530
00:54:51,872 --> 00:54:52,872
A human face.

531
00:54:56,502 --> 00:54:58,002
Carl, we're short-handed.

532
00:54:58,087 --> 00:54:59,921
I need you out on the street. Go.

533
00:55:02,549 --> 00:55:05,343
<i>Sheriff, the mayor just
arrived. He's looking for you.</i>

534
00:55:06,845 --> 00:55:07,845
Thank you.

535
00:55:08,722 --> 00:55:10,890
Have a seat. I'll be back in a minute.

536
00:55:15,354 --> 00:55:17,021
Some goddamn lunatic ruined the fair!

537
00:55:17,106 --> 00:55:19,148
I demand to know what the
police are going to do about it!

538
00:55:19,233 --> 00:55:20,233
In my office.

539
00:55:24,613 --> 00:55:25,697
I think it could be Jed.

540
00:55:26,281 --> 00:55:27,281
Jed Sawyer?

541
00:55:27,366 --> 00:55:28,950
Impossible.

542
00:55:29,034 --> 00:55:30,743
We burned that house down years ago, Hooper.

543
00:55:30,869 --> 00:55:32,286
You were there. Nobody escaped.

544
00:55:32,371 --> 00:55:34,414
Maybe he slipped out the back. I don't know.

545
00:55:34,540 --> 00:55:35,999
You're saying he's been
hiding all these years

546
00:55:36,083 --> 00:55:37,375
and now he's running loose around town?

547
00:55:37,459 --> 00:55:41,587
I'm saying a six-foot-six man
came out of Verna Carson's house

548
00:55:41,797 --> 00:55:44,549
wearing a skin mask and holding that thing.

549
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:45,883
<i>Sheriff?</i>

550
00:55:46,301 --> 00:55:47,885
I'm at the Carson house.

551
00:55:48,429 --> 00:55:49,721
<i>The gate's been forced open.</i>

552
00:55:50,556 --> 00:55:52,890
There's a broken side
mirror. It matches the van.

553
00:55:52,975 --> 00:55:54,892
Marvin, you were supposed to stay by the van.

554
00:55:55,227 --> 00:55:56,269
That's an order. Do you copy?

555
00:55:56,395 --> 00:55:57,895
Absolutely not! We're not doing it that way!

556
00:55:57,980 --> 00:55:59,981
There's a trail of blood on the pavement.

557
00:56:00,065 --> 00:56:02,150
Sheriff, with all due respect,
we have to follow the trail.

558
00:56:02,234 --> 00:56:03,943
<i>-That's not your decision, Deputy.
-Marvin!</i>

559
00:56:04,403 --> 00:56:06,571
<i>This is Mayor Hartman. Do you have your gun?</i>

560
00:56:06,780 --> 00:56:07,947
Of course. Extended magazine.

561
00:56:09,616 --> 00:56:11,075
All I need is an excuse, sir.

562
00:56:11,285 --> 00:56:12,827
Then what the hell are you waiting for?

563
00:56:13,746 --> 00:56:17,540
Marvin, stay put. We think Jed
Sawyer might still be alive.

564
00:56:17,624 --> 00:56:18,708
<i>And he might be in that house.</i>

565
00:56:18,792 --> 00:56:23,004
Copy that, sir, but a chainsaw
doesn't make him bulletproof.

566
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:56,621
LOCAL HEROES!

567
00:57:01,668 --> 00:57:04,504
ONE VICTIM ESCAPED
"He sawed up my paraplegic brother."

568
00:57:06,215 --> 00:57:11,886
Four young people brutally murdered

569
00:57:13,388 --> 00:57:14,764
Gruesome discoveries

570
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:17,683
Slaughterhouse family
turned their farm into one

571
00:57:17,810 --> 00:57:22,647
The Sawyers refused to surrender

572
00:57:22,731 --> 00:57:25,108
A deadly shootout

573
00:57:25,192 --> 00:57:32,156
The farmhouse fire

574
00:57:35,202 --> 00:57:37,495
SUNDAY, AUGUST 19

575
00:57:49,758 --> 00:57:50,842
The door's open.

576
00:57:51,510 --> 00:57:54,554
This is a mistake. Stop him
now before he gets hurt.

577
00:57:54,680 --> 00:57:56,347
<i>-It's a fresh lead, Hooper.
-I'm going in.</i>

578
00:58:01,687 --> 00:58:02,687
Police!

579
00:58:13,574 --> 00:58:14,574
Yeah.

580
00:58:14,700 --> 00:58:17,201
-I want to see.
-Sure.

581
00:58:21,373 --> 00:58:22,373
Moving forward.

582
00:58:28,547 --> 00:58:29,547
CONFIDENTIAL

583
00:58:35,637 --> 00:58:37,263
SWORN STATEMENT OF:
SHERIFF HOOPER

584
00:58:39,600 --> 00:58:43,853
The Sawyers were complying

585
00:58:43,937 --> 00:58:47,231
BURT HARTMAN
led the mob

586
00:58:47,316 --> 00:58:50,401
A shootout began

587
00:58:50,485 --> 00:58:53,946
Escalated
brutal

588
00:58:54,072 --> 00:58:55,489
Slaughter

589
00:58:55,574 --> 00:58:57,074
Burned

590
00:58:57,159 --> 00:58:58,409
Death

591
00:58:58,493 --> 00:58:59,744
Family

592
00:58:59,828 --> 00:59:01,746
Massacred

593
00:59:06,168 --> 00:59:10,254
I confronted Burt Hartman

594
00:59:12,758 --> 00:59:13,799
You're responsible for this, Burt.

595
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:16,636
An eye for an eye, Sheriff.
Nobody escapes biblical justice.

596
00:59:18,263 --> 00:59:21,682
Nobody escapes biblical justice

597
00:59:25,145 --> 00:59:26,145
<i>Entering the kitchen.</i>

598
00:59:26,647 --> 00:59:27,647
Proceed.

599
00:59:35,113 --> 00:59:36,280
What the hell is that?

600
00:59:40,953 --> 00:59:42,453
<i>I'm following the blood.</i>

601
00:59:46,458 --> 00:59:47,458
Jesus!

602
00:59:49,878 --> 00:59:50,878
Are you seeing this?

603
00:59:51,713 --> 00:59:52,713
Shit.

604
00:59:57,135 --> 00:59:59,011
Looks like it leads to this door.

605
01:00:00,347 --> 01:00:01,347
<i>Open it.</i>

606
01:00:09,856 --> 01:00:10,982
What the hell is this?

607
01:00:11,525 --> 01:00:12,692
<i>Proceed, Deputy.</i>

608
01:00:18,156 --> 01:00:19,407
I don't know if I should, Burt.

609
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:21,492
Goddamn it. Do I have to come hold your hand?

610
01:00:50,188 --> 01:00:51,188
<i>Where are you now?</i>

611
01:00:51,356 --> 01:00:52,565
<i>In the cellar.</i>

612
01:00:59,197 --> 01:01:00,865
There's an opening to some kind of...

613
01:01:03,618 --> 01:01:04,618
I don't know.

614
01:01:07,456 --> 01:01:08,456
I'm going in.

615
01:01:13,962 --> 01:01:17,423
Looks like some really weird catacomb.

616
01:01:21,928 --> 01:01:23,429
Still following the blood.

617
01:01:36,610 --> 01:01:38,903
I've got a bad feeling about this.

618
01:01:57,923 --> 01:01:59,590
Holy shit. What is this?

619
01:02:06,765 --> 01:02:07,765
Is this a shelter?

620
01:02:20,946 --> 01:02:21,946
Dresses.

621
01:02:27,285 --> 01:02:28,285
High heels.

622
01:02:30,163 --> 01:02:31,539
<i>Little farm toys.</i>

623
01:02:32,290 --> 01:02:33,290
<i>Bones.</i>

624
01:02:33,959 --> 01:02:34,959
<i>Jesus.</i>

625
01:02:40,465 --> 01:02:44,635
Women's makeup? What a freak.

626
01:02:53,061 --> 01:02:55,062
VICTIM: LORETTA SAWYER
AGE: UNKNOWN — AUGUST 19

627
01:03:13,665 --> 01:03:19,044
Loretta Sawyer — F
Age 27, single, daughter not found

628
01:03:19,171 --> 01:03:21,672
Presumed dead

629
01:03:27,345 --> 01:03:30,181
<i>I've never been in a place this disturbing.</i>

630
01:03:30,390 --> 01:03:31,515
What's to your left?

631
01:03:32,184 --> 01:03:33,142
A door.

632
01:03:33,226 --> 01:03:34,685
<i>Marvin, keep your gun ready!</i>

633
01:03:40,066 --> 01:03:41,859
Oh, God. Shit.

634
01:03:43,528 --> 01:03:44,528
<i>How many?</i>

635
01:03:46,531 --> 01:03:48,157
<i>You tell me.</i>

636
01:03:48,241 --> 01:03:49,700
Who the fuck could do something like this?

637
01:03:53,872 --> 01:03:56,040
Shit, this is horrible.

638
01:04:01,046 --> 01:04:02,046
What's in there?

639
01:04:02,380 --> 01:04:03,380
<i>What's in the freezer?</i>

640
01:04:08,595 --> 01:04:09,720
<i>Be careful, Marvin.</i>

641
01:04:31,493 --> 01:04:32,493
Shit!

642
01:04:32,577 --> 01:04:33,577
Calm down! That didn't happen!

643
01:04:33,828 --> 01:04:35,871
Marvin! Get out of there right now!

644
01:04:35,956 --> 01:04:37,248
CONNECTION LOST

645
01:04:40,418 --> 01:04:41,919
That sick bastard will
come back there tonight.

646
01:04:42,337 --> 01:04:44,797
Let's round up the boys and
burn the whole house down!

647
01:04:44,923 --> 01:04:47,299
Let's finish this! Finish
what we started years ago.

648
01:04:47,801 --> 01:04:49,510
Not this time. Not on my watch!

649
01:05:39,352 --> 01:05:42,479
-What happened that day was a disgrace.
-We delivered justice!

650
01:05:44,316 --> 01:05:45,441
I want to see the Sawyer girl.

651
01:05:45,984 --> 01:05:48,360
She's a victim, Burt!
She hasn't done anything!

652
01:05:48,987 --> 01:05:51,030
She's breathing, isn't she?

653
01:05:58,371 --> 01:06:00,623
MURDERERS

654
01:06:02,500 --> 01:06:03,709
Yeah, I know what you're thinking, Burt.

655
01:06:03,835 --> 01:06:05,002
You have no idea!

656
01:06:07,464 --> 01:06:09,548
That girl had better not get hurt, Burt!

657
01:06:25,649 --> 01:06:26,774
Hello, Farnsworth speaking.

658
01:06:26,858 --> 01:06:28,025
Hi. This is Heather Miller.

659
01:06:29,027 --> 01:06:32,613
All my friends have been murdered. I
found out what happened on August 19.

660
01:06:32,697 --> 01:06:34,156
How could you leave us alone in that house?

661
01:06:34,240 --> 01:06:36,659
All right. Where are you?

662
01:06:37,202 --> 01:06:38,702
At the bank on Main Street.

663
01:06:39,496 --> 01:06:42,665
Meet me at Johnny B. Red's
bar, about a quarter mile

664
01:06:42,749 --> 01:06:44,792
<i>east of Fifth and Main.</i>

665
01:06:44,876 --> 01:06:46,043
I'll be there in 20 minutes.

666
01:06:48,380 --> 01:06:50,923
I want your Halloween candy!

667
01:06:51,049 --> 01:06:52,424
Come celebrate with us!

668
01:08:58,635 --> 01:08:59,760
Why didn't you warn me?

669
01:08:59,844 --> 01:09:03,305
All my friends are dead. This
crazy town destroyed my family.

670
01:09:03,389 --> 01:09:05,682
-Did you read Verna's letter?
-No.

671
01:09:06,309 --> 01:09:08,143
I asked you to, didn't I?

672
01:09:09,521 --> 01:09:12,189
Verna was very thorough. I'm
sure she explained everything.

673
01:09:12,398 --> 01:09:15,400
But you knew about him. You knew
about this town. You knew everything.

674
01:09:15,527 --> 01:09:16,527
All right.

675
01:09:17,237 --> 01:09:18,403
Then who is he?

676
01:09:19,280 --> 01:09:22,741
The person in the basement

677
01:09:24,202 --> 01:09:25,744
is Jedidiah Sawyer.

678
01:09:26,454 --> 01:09:27,454
They call him Jed.

679
01:09:28,373 --> 01:09:29,456
He's your cousin.

680
01:09:31,125 --> 01:09:34,503
I suspected something for years,
but I wasn't sure about Jed

681
01:09:34,587 --> 01:09:37,381
until four months ago, when Verna,

682
01:09:38,758 --> 01:09:41,552
who was very sick, introduced me to him.

683
01:09:42,220 --> 01:09:45,722
A huge grown man, but mentally disabled,

684
01:09:46,933 --> 01:09:49,476
with the mind of an eight-year-old child.

685
01:09:50,812 --> 01:09:52,604
To be honest, he scared me to death.

686
01:09:53,481 --> 01:09:54,481
Why did she take care of him?

687
01:09:56,150 --> 01:09:58,569
Nobody loves you like family.

688
01:09:58,778 --> 01:10:00,237
She took care of you, too.

689
01:10:01,239 --> 01:10:04,116
She looked into everyone involved

690
01:10:04,909 --> 01:10:05,993
in what happened on August nineteenth.

691
01:10:06,619 --> 01:10:09,079
-She found you right away.
-And let me live with those people?

692
01:10:09,581 --> 01:10:10,956
You were safer there.

693
01:10:12,458 --> 01:10:15,335
And she always knew this day would come.

694
01:10:16,754 --> 01:10:18,255
Jed knows about you, too.

695
01:10:18,756 --> 01:10:19,798
Some welcome.

696
01:10:22,260 --> 01:10:24,094
He doesn't know who you are.

697
01:10:24,345 --> 01:10:27,973
And the last time a girl escaped
from him, he lost his entire family.

698
01:10:28,099 --> 01:10:30,976
That's why he's hunting you.
He doesn't know any other way.

699
01:10:31,311 --> 01:10:32,603
Neither does Burt Hartman.

700
01:10:33,646 --> 01:10:37,941
Now that you've read that police file,
you know this town's dirty secret.

701
01:10:41,779 --> 01:10:44,531
-Burt!
-Yeah!

702
01:10:45,783 --> 01:10:46,783
Let me through.

703
01:10:46,951 --> 01:10:48,452
Let's go. I'm getting you out of here.

704
01:10:49,454 --> 01:10:50,454
-Move!
-Hey!

705
01:10:50,705 --> 01:10:52,664
-Get out of my way!
-What's wrong with you?

706
01:10:52,957 --> 01:10:54,374
Use the back door. Take this!

707
01:10:55,627 --> 01:10:57,044
Burt.

708
01:11:11,184 --> 01:11:12,893
I got her, Burt!

709
01:11:15,480 --> 01:11:16,480
Here she is.

710
01:11:18,316 --> 01:11:20,150
Going somewhere, sweetheart?

711
01:11:25,657 --> 01:11:28,075
He cut me! Burt!

712
01:11:32,538 --> 01:11:36,166
Little bitch. She's not
getting far, that's for sure.

713
01:11:37,085 --> 01:11:38,377
Come on. Get up!

714
01:11:44,258 --> 01:11:47,094
Stop!

715
01:11:49,931 --> 01:11:50,931
What's going on?

716
01:11:51,015 --> 01:11:52,391
Burt Hartman and his men

717
01:11:52,517 --> 01:11:55,352
attacked my lawyer at the
bar. And they're after me.

718
01:11:56,854 --> 01:11:58,438
Come on. I'll give you a ride.

719
01:11:59,357 --> 01:12:01,274
We have to stop at the
bar. We have to go back.

720
01:12:01,359 --> 01:12:02,401
All right.

721
01:12:16,541 --> 01:12:18,166
There he is. That's Farnsworth.

722
01:12:18,251 --> 01:12:19,710
That's the place! Stop the car!

723
01:12:20,128 --> 01:12:21,128
Stop the car!

724
01:12:21,713 --> 01:12:22,879
That's the bar! Stop!

725
01:12:23,047 --> 01:12:24,423
Let me out! What are you doing?

726
01:12:27,468 --> 01:12:29,052
Stop the damn car!

727
01:12:29,220 --> 01:12:30,262
What are you doing?

728
01:12:32,974 --> 01:12:33,974
Yeah?

729
01:12:34,058 --> 01:12:36,059
The Sawyer girl escaped.
She's headed toward town.

730
01:12:36,269 --> 01:12:38,603
Yeah. I've got her. I'm taking her out back.

731
01:12:38,730 --> 01:12:39,771
What do you want me to do with her?

732
01:12:39,897 --> 01:12:43,400
<i>Take her to the slaughterhouse
and keep her there.</i>

733
01:12:44,610 --> 01:12:47,612
I'm dealing with Ollie.
She cut him pretty bad.

734
01:12:48,281 --> 01:12:49,573
<i>Give me a few minutes.</i>

735
01:12:50,408 --> 01:12:51,408
All right.

736
01:12:51,576 --> 01:12:52,576
Sure, Dad.

737
01:12:54,287 --> 01:12:55,787
He's your dad, you bastard?

738
01:12:57,749 --> 01:12:59,249
Stop the damn car!

739
01:12:59,584 --> 01:13:00,584
Let me out!

740
01:13:00,835 --> 01:13:03,336
Open the door, you liar!

741
01:13:06,591 --> 01:13:11,094
<i>Marvin, do you copy? We've got
the girl from the Carson house.</i>

742
01:13:12,013 --> 01:13:15,599
<i>Come on, Marvin, answer. Are
you there? Come on, Marvin.</i>

743
01:13:18,811 --> 01:13:21,772
<i>Is that you, Marvin? If you can hear me,</i>

744
01:13:22,106 --> 01:13:23,482
<i>meet us at the slaughterhouse.</i>

745
01:13:40,208 --> 01:13:43,460
Sheriff, I represent Verna Carson's
estate and her granddaughter, Heather.

746
01:13:43,628 --> 01:13:44,586
I know who she is.

747
01:13:44,670 --> 01:13:48,298
Right now, she's in one of your
patrol cars, against her will,

748
01:13:48,382 --> 01:13:50,509
leaving town. They passed
Johnny B. Red's bar.

749
01:13:50,802 --> 01:13:51,802
All right, come with me.

750
01:13:55,473 --> 01:13:57,224
He's heading for Highway 28.

751
01:13:58,309 --> 01:13:59,476
There's nothing out there.

752
01:14:01,813 --> 01:14:04,064
Shit. I know where he's going.

753
01:14:16,327 --> 01:14:17,327
You know,

754
01:14:19,664 --> 01:14:21,915
I thought you were a nice guy.

755
01:14:31,717 --> 01:14:33,343
So you're a Hartman?

756
01:14:35,555 --> 01:14:36,555
Yeah.

757
01:14:44,355 --> 01:14:45,438
Well, I'm a Sawyer.

758
01:15:04,542 --> 01:15:05,542
Please, stop!

759
01:15:26,814 --> 01:15:27,981
Stop it!

760
01:15:38,910 --> 01:15:39,910
Don't tempt me.

761
01:15:42,788 --> 01:15:44,664
You should feel right at
home in this awful place.

762
01:15:45,625 --> 01:15:47,626
Your family used to work in this filth.

763
01:16:55,069 --> 01:16:58,405
Leave her to us. This is
no place for a cop, son.

764
01:17:45,202 --> 01:17:46,202
It's me!

765
01:17:46,579 --> 01:17:47,579
I'm Heather!

766
01:17:48,247 --> 01:17:49,331
I'm your cousin!

767
01:17:49,415 --> 01:17:51,583
It's me! I'm Heather!

768
01:17:52,251 --> 01:17:53,710
Please, it's Heather!

769
01:18:04,472 --> 01:18:06,181
Come here. Remember me?

770
01:18:15,358 --> 01:18:17,609
Come on, Ollie. Let's put
him in the grinder. Hurry!

771
01:18:17,693 --> 01:18:18,693
Hit him, Burt.

772
01:18:18,778 --> 01:18:20,236
Come here! Move your big ass!

773
01:18:20,488 --> 01:18:21,488
Get up there!

774
01:18:24,617 --> 01:18:26,284
You're going to die, bastard.

775
01:18:31,374 --> 01:18:32,374
Hurry!

776
01:18:34,835 --> 01:18:37,045
Tonight I'm going to wipe out
the entire Sawyer bloodline.

777
01:18:37,129 --> 01:18:38,922
You and that pretty little
bitch cousin of yours.

778
01:18:39,965 --> 01:18:41,132
That's right, Burt. Hit him again.

779
01:18:42,927 --> 01:18:45,178
You're about to die, bastard.

780
01:18:45,596 --> 01:18:47,097
Son of a bitch!

781
01:18:47,181 --> 01:18:49,265
-Get that chain, Ollie.
-Okay. Right away, Burt.

782
01:18:52,144 --> 01:18:53,895
You're a grotesque excuse for a man.

783
01:18:54,438 --> 01:18:55,772
You're not getting away that easily.

784
01:18:56,065 --> 01:18:57,524
I'm going to enjoy this, you hear me?

785
01:18:57,775 --> 01:18:59,150
-Hurry up, Ollie.
-It's ready.

786
01:18:59,276 --> 01:19:00,276
Give me that.

787
01:19:03,280 --> 01:19:05,073
You're going to be ground up like a damn cow!

788
01:19:05,157 --> 01:19:07,450
You'll be turned into pig feed.

789
01:19:09,870 --> 01:19:12,664
-Turn it on, Ollie. Come on.
-All right, Burt. Right away!

790
01:19:12,748 --> 01:19:13,998
You can count on that.

791
01:19:14,875 --> 01:19:16,418
I'm going to enjoy watching it chew you up.

792
01:19:24,301 --> 01:19:27,262
You're a son of a bitch. This is
my town, you fucking cockroach.

793
01:19:27,721 --> 01:19:28,721
It's running, Burt!

794
01:19:32,101 --> 01:19:34,811
Of all the Sawyers, all you sick bastards,

795
01:19:34,937 --> 01:19:37,355
the only one who gets out of
the fire is a goddamn retard?

796
01:19:37,565 --> 01:19:38,815
How the hell did that happen?

797
01:19:41,152 --> 01:19:42,152
Remember me?

798
01:19:55,082 --> 01:19:57,250
You got nine lives like a cat?

799
01:19:57,334 --> 01:20:01,129
You came back. But today you'll
die, bastard, just like your daddy.

800
01:20:01,589 --> 01:20:03,047
Your day has come!

801
01:20:14,268 --> 01:20:15,268
Hey!

802
01:20:15,811 --> 01:20:16,811
-Idiot!
-Hey!

803
01:20:17,605 --> 01:20:18,605
Hey!

804
01:20:20,316 --> 01:20:21,524
Look who's back.

805
01:20:22,234 --> 01:20:23,693
That's right.

806
01:20:26,989 --> 01:20:28,406
Do your thing, cuz.

807
01:20:38,709 --> 01:20:39,709
Cockroach.

808
01:20:40,920 --> 01:20:41,961
Bitch, you're dead.

809
01:20:42,379 --> 01:20:43,379
I'm going to tear you to pieces, you hear me?

810
01:20:43,464 --> 01:20:44,631
You worthless scum.

811
01:21:15,746 --> 01:21:16,746
Thank God, Hooper!

812
01:21:17,206 --> 01:21:18,206
Shoot him!

813
01:21:18,666 --> 01:21:20,542
Come on, shoot him!

814
01:21:20,626 --> 01:21:21,626
Don't shoot!

815
01:21:21,710 --> 01:21:23,336
Hooper! Finish him!

816
01:21:24,421 --> 01:21:26,422
Shoot the idiot. Kill him!

817
01:21:28,008 --> 01:21:30,260
Pull the trigger, you
spineless son of a bitch!

818
01:21:30,594 --> 01:21:31,844
He's going to kill me!

819
01:21:32,888 --> 01:21:33,888
God!

820
01:21:33,973 --> 01:21:34,973
Don't shoot!

821
01:21:35,057 --> 01:21:38,017
Hooper! Finish what we started!

822
01:22:04,878 --> 01:22:07,505
Nobody escapes biblical justice, Burt.

823
01:22:17,516 --> 01:22:18,725
Clean up this mess.

824
01:24:23,767 --> 01:24:25,268
<i>Dear granddaughter:</i>

825
01:24:26,603 --> 01:24:30,273
<i>This house and everything
in it now belong to you.</i>

826
01:24:31,859 --> 01:24:35,778
<i>But you should know that these gifts
come with certain responsibilities.</i>

827
01:24:37,698 --> 01:24:41,576
<i>Your real name is Edith Rose Sawyer.</i>

828
01:24:44,371 --> 01:24:47,957
<i>I instructed Farnsworth to give
you a set of keys to the estate.</i>

829
01:24:48,459 --> 01:24:52,128
<i>The big key opens the
reinforced door to the cellar.</i>

830
01:24:52,796 --> 01:24:55,923
<i>There you'll find a metal door.</i>

831
01:24:56,467 --> 01:24:58,509
<i>Behind it lives your cousin,</i>

832
01:24:59,094 --> 01:25:00,261
<i>Jedidiah Sawyer,</i>

833
01:25:01,930 --> 01:25:04,766
<i>the only blood relative you have left.</i>

834
01:25:05,434 --> 01:25:08,644
<i>He is devoted to the family
and will protect you.</i>

835
01:25:09,521 --> 01:25:12,440
<i>In return, he only asks
that you care for him.</i>

836
01:25:14,985 --> 01:25:19,280
<i>Edith, you are the last
of the Sawyer bloodline.</i>

837
01:25:21,158 --> 01:25:23,409
<i>My blood runs through your veins.</i>

838
01:25:25,287 --> 01:25:28,080
<i>Whether you stay is your choice.</i>

839
01:25:29,041 --> 01:25:31,918
<i>But remember, you are a Sawyer,</i>

840
01:25:32,503 --> 01:25:34,337
<i>and this is your home.</i>

841
01:26:33,647 --> 01:26:36,274
<i>It's your time.</i>

842
01:31:31,486 --> 01:31:34,321
Remember to tell her you love her.

843
01:31:36,032 --> 01:31:39,326
With all the money she
has now, it's almost true.

844
01:31:39,932 --> 01:32:29,326
